# Andok's Website Menu

> A responsive, static menu page for an Andok's website, with a hero carousel, scrollable food categories, dish cards, and a dark mode toggle.

---

## Features

- **Hero carousel**: auto-sliding banner with three image slides, prev/next arrows, and dot indicators
- **Category selector**: horizontally scrollable, snap-to-item row of circular category images
- **Dish cards**: image, title, and description cards with hover lift and zoom effects
- **Bestseller ribbon**: highlight special items with a "BESTSELLER" corner ribbon
- **Quick view**: hover button and modal for a closer look at a dish
- **Dark mode**: sun/moon toggle that restyles the whole page
- **Scroll-to-top button**: jump back to the top on long pages
- **Responsive design**: layout adjusts across desktop, tablet, and mobile breakpoints
- **Shared layout**: a reusable `layout.html` with the navbar

## Tech Stack

- HTML5, CSS3, and vanilla JavaScript
- [Bootstrap 5.3.6](https://getbootstrap.com/) (via CDN)
- [Bootstrap Icons 1.10.5](https://icons.getbootstrap.com/) (via CDN)

## Project Structure

```
Andoks-Website-Menu/
├── Images/         # Hero slides and menu photos
├── img/            # Additional images and icons
├── css/
│   └── layout.css  # Shared layout and navbar styles
├── layout.html     # Shared page layout / navbar
├── menu.html       # Main menu page
└── README.md
```

> The default branch is `andoksmainmenu`.

## Getting Started

No build step or server is required.

1. **Clone the repository**
   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/HiraiGinji/Andoks-Website-Menu.git
   cd Andoks-Website-Menu
   git checkout andoksmainmenu
   ```

2. **Open the site**
   - Double-click `menu.html` to open it in your browser, **or**
   - Serve it locally for best results:
     ```bash
     # Python
     python -m http.server 8000
     # or Node
     npx serve
     ```
     Then visit `http://localhost:8000/menu.html`.

> An internet connection is needed on first load for the Bootstrap and Bootstrap Icons CDNs.

## Customization

| What to change      | Where                                                         |
| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Hero slide images   | `.hero-slide:nth-child(n)::before` rules in `menu.html`       |
| Menu categories     | The `.menu-selector` section in `menu.html`                   |
| Dish cards          | The `.dish-cards` section in `menu.html`                      |
| Brand colors        | Red `#d32f2f` / `#b71c1c` and yellow `#ffc107` in the styles  |
| Navbar              | `layout.html` and `css/layout.css`                            |
| Dark mode colors    | The `.dark-mode` rules in `menu.html`                         |

To mark a dish as a bestseller, add the `special` class to its card:

```html
<div class="dish-card special">...</div>
```

## Browser Support

Works in current versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox, and Safari.
